    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4242bbf5-374b-46d0-8aab-4673d3a22506\n\nI am not sure if this is a Neovim bug. I tried tmux and Alacritty, and no flicker occurs there.\n\nI’m not sure this is a Neovim bug. I observe no flicker in tmux and Alacritty, but the flicker occurs in Kitty. Since vanilla Vim does not have this issue, I’m filing this report and will close it if the root cause is unrelated to Neovim.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nI can reproduce this with both `nvim --clean` and `nvim -u NONE`. The top‑area flicker occurs on file save even without any user configuration.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nNo flicker\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-4886416\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nNo\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nLinux 7.1.9-arch1-2\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nkitty 0.48.2\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-kitty\n\n### Installation\n\nbuild from repo",
